Microsoft Intune: Win32 Application Deployment and Uninstallation

Project Overview

In this practical lab, I used Microsoft Intune to deploy and uninstall a Win32 application on a Windows 11 virtual machine.

The application used for this exercise was 7-Zip 26.02 (x64 edition). I packaged the application for deployment through Intune, configured application assignments, and tested the installation and uninstallation workflows.

The purpose of this project was to understand how IT administrators can manage application deployment and removal on Windows devices using Microsoft Intune.

Lab Environment

* Device: Windows 11 virtual machine
* Virtualization platform: VMware Workstation Player
* Endpoint management platform: Microsoft Intune admin center
* Application: 7-Zip 26.02 (x64 edition)
* Application type: Windows Win32 application
* Deployment package: 7z2602-x64.intunewin
* Test group: HR-GROUP

Practical Objectives

1. Package a Windows application for deployment through Intune.
2. Configure a Win32 application in the Intune admin center.
3. Configure application assignments.
4. Test the application installation workflow.
5. Configure an uninstallation assignment for HR-GROUP.
6. Monitor application deployment status through Intune reporting.

Implementation Steps

1. Prepare the Application

I prepared the 7-Zip application package for deployment through Microsoft Intune.

The package used was:

7z2602-x64.intunewin

2. Configure the Win32 Application

I configured 7-Zip as a Win32 application in the Microsoft Intune admin center.

I reviewed the application configuration and assignment settings.

3. Configure the Installation Assignment

I configured an installation assignment under the Required deployment category.

This assignment is intended to make the application install automatically on targeted devices.

4. Configure the Uninstallation Assignment

I configured an uninstallation assignment targeting HR-GROUP.

This allowed me to practise controlling application removal through Intune group assignments.

5. Test Installation and Uninstallation

I tested the installation and uninstallation workflows on my Windows 11 lab environment.

Both operations behaved as expected during my practical testing.

6. Monitor Deployment Status

I navigated to the application’s monitoring section in Intune and inspected the Device install status and User install status reports.

The reports continued to display Not installed for the targeted device at the time of documentation, despite the successful practical tests.

This highlighted an important endpoint management lesson: an application’s observed state on a device and its reported state in Intune should be verified separately.

Further investigation may be necessary to confirm reporting synchronization, assignment scope, and application detection settings.

